  "Measured 2026-10-08 on bh-glx-110-d07u08 (RevC, 130 W), tree b583043bcf4 with no experiment knobs. Per chunk size: one tracy capture of a global and a sliding layer at chunk index 1 (dense = everything but SDPA), and one host-timed replay of each layer at every chunk index to 256k (global attention slope).",
  "Dense time per step (60 layers): 54.8 / 46.0 / 62.7 / 89.4 / 181 ms at 128 / 256 / 512 / 1024 / 2048 rows per device. Below 256 rows it gets slower, not faster (the short-slab paths are keyed to chunk 2048). Past 1024 rows it stops getting cheaper per row.",
  "Global attention per layer is a line in prefix depth per chunk size, fitted over every depth (max residual 69 \u00b5s at 1k and 2k, 0.6\u20130.9 ms at 8k and 16k). Sliding attention is flat with depth and includes the halo.",
  "Device time at full clock. Long runs sit under the 130 W cap (\u22123 to \u22128% at 256k on RevC); the model has no clock term.",
  "The last chunk of every prompt is padded to the unit (fixed trace shapes). Under Pack a request's piece is k units wide, so serving would need a trace per slot layout and per-request chunk widths.",
  "Batched ring attention with several requests per call and per-request halos don't exist yet. These are planning numbers, to be checked against the batching PoC."
